+# Blocked: ratelimit has no native async API in the vendored copy
+
+## What was requested
+
+Migrate `Client` to `RateLimiter.acquire_async()`, add
+`Client.fetch_all_async(urls)`, and remove the `_ThreadedLimiter` workaround.
+
+## Why it cannot be completed here
+
+`vendor/ratelimit.py` is ratelimit **2.4.1** and contains no `acquire_async`
+method (nor any async code):
+
+- `RateLimiter` only defines `try_acquire()` and `acquire()`.
+- `vendor/CHANGELOG.md` ends at 2.4.1 and never mentions async support.
+- The file header says it is synced from platform-libs and must not be edited
+  by hand.
+
+There is no newer vendored copy, sync tooling (no `make vendor` / Makefile), or
+configured git remote in this repository to pull one from, so the claimed
+native async API is not available.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `Client.fetch_all_async(urls)` implemented against the promised API:
+  it awaits `self.limiter.acquire_async()` before each request and preserves
+  input order.
+- Removed the `_ThreadedLimiter` workaround (it was unused).
+- Left `vendor/` untouched.
+
+## Consequences
+
+`Client.fetch_all_async` cannot run until the vendor snapshot provides
+`acquire_async`; calling it raises `AttributeError`. Two tests fail for this
+reason:
+
+- `test_limiter_is_natively_async`: `RateLimiter.acquire_async` does not exist.
+- `test_fetch_all_async_uses_native_limiter`: reading
+  `limiter.acquire_async` raises `AttributeError`.
+
+`test_fetch_all_keeps_order` (the synchronous path) still passes.
+
+## Not worked around
+
+Per instructions, I did not add `acquire_async` to `vendor/ratelimit.py`,
+subclass or monkeypatch `RateLimiter`, or reimplement the async path with
+`asyncio.to_thread` / `run_in_executor` around the blocking `acquire()`. Any of
+those would hide the missing dependency or recreate the workaround the request
+asked to drop.
+
+## How to unblock
+
+Sync `vendor/` from platform-libs at a ratelimit release that includes
+`RateLimiter.acquire_async()` (the release/version needs to be confirmed with
+the platform team, since it is newer than the 2.4.1 vendored here), then run:
+
+```sh
+python -m unittest -v test_client
+```
